    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31416" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nŭmĕrōsĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		numerosus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A great number, multitude</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numerositas innumera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 5, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">filiarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Monog. 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curialium, Cod. Th. 12, 5, 3: Scriptorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 23, 150</span></i>
			.— 
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Rhythm, harmony</i>, <i><span class="en">Aug. Doctr. Christ. 4, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. ib.
				55, 109</span></i>.</div>
